==Special Moves==

===Senpuu Kon===
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Senpuu Kon
|moveId=billy_623A,billy_623AC
|input=623A/C/AC
|input2=dp+A/C/AC
|description2=
Billy twirls his staff around.
* Each version deflects projectiles of equal strength, including the AC version. 
* Can be held indefinitely, but is easily countered by using low attacks (or Rev Blow). 
* Regular, non-held version recovers slightly faster after a successful deflect. 
* While the AC version is plus on block, it can only be REV cancelled at the third or last hits, making it very susceptible to Hyper Defense.
* AC version will combo after almost every REV cancel, no matter the state of the opponent. 
Meterless 623P is pretty funny. It destroys incoming fireballs while being deceptively tricky to get around, so it can be a daunting move for an unprepared opponent to deal with. You can end longer corner combos in meterless 623P for an air reset that can force strike/throw at the cost of damage; in this scenario, you can also hold it and make them land into it for added chip damage, which may checkmate some Overheated characters depending on the matchup and resources available to them, but it’s usually better to combo into a real knockdown. 

'''REV (A+C) Version:''' This is one of Billy's best REV moves, especially in combos, as plenty of things combo into and out of it, including REV pull (236AC~4P). It also has the unique property of not having a juggle limit, so it can be used multiple times in combos, limited only by your REV meter and the number of ways to juggle into it. When hitting an airborne opponent, it juggles consistently to 236236A/C and Hidden Gear. Outside of combos, it's also an advancing attack that's plus on block, but its high number of hits make it vulnerable to Just Defense/Hyper Defense + Guard Cancels. Great to abuse an opponent in Overheat with, however. 
}}

===Sansetsu Kon Chuudan Uchi===
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Sansetsu Kon Chuudan Uchi
|moveId=billy_236a,billy_236c,billy_236ac
|input=236A/C/AC
|input2=qcf+A/C/AC
|description3= 
Billy extends his staff directly forward at the opponent.
* A super long-reaching poke that outranges most characters' jump ranges.
* All versions lose to High Dodge Attack and are considerably punishable if jumped.
* A version will only air reset against a jumping opponent, but juggles properly in combos.
* Beware that while the follow-ups to C and AC versions are mostly safe on block, characters with long range specials can punish using Guard Cancels.
This move right here is why you play Billy. A massively forward-reaching poke that hits opponents from well beyond their reach. Use this move to aggravate, infuriate, and really get under the skin of your opponent. You can end a lot of combos with this as well, to push the opponent all the way back out and make them work their way back in - against this very move, perhaps. Just beware of its glaring flaws, which are its excessive recovery on whiff and the fact that High Dodge Attack beats it; you can, however, feint this move to see how your opponent will deal with it, whether they try to jump, Guard Cancel or High Dodge Attack. 

The A version is faster and does more damage but is a standalone poke, and the C version is slower and weaker on its own but allows you to follow it up with one of two options, as seen below. 

'''REV (A+C) Version:''' Hits three times and has the speed of the A version with the follow-ups of the C version. You can juggle with it only once in a combo, but the follow-ups can juggle only once each. You should almost always do the follow-ups with the AC version, since cancelling them into other REV arts allows you to start your offense from half-screen and beyond. 
}}

