* No invulnerability, but combos from the High Dodge Attack for anti-air combos. 
* A version will only air reset against a jumping opponent, but juggles properly in combos.
* C version launches on Counter Hit. 
Basically the same move as 236A/C, but angled upward to hit airborne opponents. It doesn't hit grounded opponents at all. It's difficult to use this move on reaction to a jumping opponent, but it's possible thanks to its faster startup; however you'll often combo into this rather than anti-air with it. If you combo into this in the corner, you can almost always continue the combo afterward, usually into a 214B/D or super.

'''REV (A+C) Version:''' Hits twice and launches slightly higher, even if you don't do its followup. You will always want to do the followup, though, for the sake of combos. 
}}

