The infamous wheel of death. Billy spins his staff as he conjures a ring of flames, then slings that ring at the opponent. 
* Hits behind Billy as well; even when this happens, he will still launch them forward.
* All hits nullify projectiles, even other projectile supers like Terry’s Power Geyser.
* Does not reach from the max range of close C. 
* The final hit launches on Counter Hit, but has additional scaling.
A very strong reversal super and, when in range, devastating combo ender. The forward-moving fire ring can catch opponents off guard if they’re too far out to block and punish, but a well-timed jump-in will go over this.
-----
'''A Version''': Does high damage and is fast for a basic super, has great okizeme, works in all corner juggles. All-around amazing super that you will want to use in combos, sometimes as a reversal, or even as an anti-air under the right circumstances.
<br>Its range is a bit of an issue. However, in some juggles, such as after 236BD, you can either do 623AC into this move to score damage at the cost of REV. If you don’t want to spend REV, you can cancel dash into this super from certain juggles by using the dash macro, which is done by inputting 236Rev > 236A.
-----
'''C Version:''' Deals a bit more damage and has better startup, which makes it work in more combos. However, it’s worse than the A version in almost every other way. The range is identical. Unless you need the extra damage to close out the round, it’s better to stick to the level 1 version, keeping your extra bar just in case. 
}}

